## Root cause
`padStart` in `/luxon/src/impl/util.js` padded the *string form of the signed number*:

```js
export function padStart(input, n = 2) {
  if (input.toString().length < n) {
    return ("0".repeat(n) + input).slice(-n);   // "-1" -> "00-1" -> slice(-4) -> "00-1"
  } else {
    return input.toString();
  }
}
```

Two defects: (1) the minus sign is counted as a digit, so `"0".repeat(n) + "-1"` = `"0000-1"` and `slice(-4)` yields `"00-1"` (zeros land *after* the sign); (2) `slice(-n)` can also chop the sign off. Result: `DateTime.utc(-1,1,1).toISODate() === "00-1-01-01"`, `toISO() === "00-1-01-01T00:00:00.000Z"`, and `-100` was left unpadded (`"-100-01-01"`).

## Fix (only `/luxon/src/impl/util.js`, padStart hunk)
```diff
 export function padStart(input, n = 2) {
-  if (input.toString().length < n) {
-    return ("0".repeat(n) + input).slice(-n);
+  const isNeg = input < 0;
+  const target = isNeg ? -input : input;
+  if (target.toString().length < n) {
+    return (isNeg ? "-" : "") + ("0".repeat(n) + target).slice(-n);
   } else {
-    return input.toString();
+    return (isNeg ? "-" : "") + target.toString();
   }
 }
```
Padding is applied to the absolute value and the sign is re-attached in front; the `else` branch is preserved so numbers already at/over width are never truncated (`padStart(-12345,4) === "-12345"`). Note: `git diff src/impl/util.js` also shows an `objToLocalTS` hunk — that is **another subagent's** change, not mine; I only edited the `padStart` function.

